						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1142.msg11283#msg11283"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1142.msg11283#msg11283">Re: New content not worth it?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #5 on:</b> September 19, 2004, 07:21:07 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							No offense but the original Epics were just that - they were quests of epical propotion.  They were quests that were long and difficult to complete.  They were not quests that middle or lower guilds were supposed to conquer.  It was only after quite some time that the epics were easy enough for everyone to compelte.  You cannot expect that the new ones will be easy either.  Heck some of them have yet to be discovered yet.  These are going to be difficult quests and even more difficult fights to complete.  When the original epics came out they were a status symbol and I&#039;m sure this time much will be the same.  It just goes to logic.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
