	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg11332"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=52" title="View the profile of Gabus">Gabus</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Drolvarg Guardian<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 276<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/psychotic-day.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I beat the Internet. The end guy was hard.<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=52"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1142.msg11332#msg11332"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1142.msg11332#msg11332">Re: New content not worth it?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #8 on:</b> September 21, 2004, 10:39:01 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							People are forgetting how bloody hard the original epics were back in the day. The paladin epic STILL is difficult if you dont have a dedicated team of 65&#039;s to pull it off, and who wants to do that since it bites so bad. Take the original firey avenger, put into the game when the original 3 planes were introduced.<br /><br />Forget all the original bullshit part of the quest getting soulfire, that part alone was more involved than almost any other quest in the game at the time. The hardest part about killing lucan was finding 46-50th level players who were willing to screw their freeport faction forever by killing him. With FP being the only good aligned town anywhere near the only two high level zones (Sol B and LGuk) many were unwilling to take away a convenient zone to help you get a cool flamey sword.<br /><br />Kill Nagafen and Vox. A massive undertaking when the level cap was 50, the best common haste gear was an FBSS, the best armor non-uber folks could hope for was class armor, (who else had a full set of armor of ro.. come on.. i know you are out there) and a generally held mantra was stats&gt;ac or hp. A public raid required 2-3 hours of prep minimum because we didnt have all the nifty raid tools you whippersnappers have today. Even then, winning was NOT guarenteed, and a CR was a nasty. (or expensive proposition) Only after that did you have a CHANCE at your epic piece IF it dropped. Then you had to repeat this again for Vox.<br /><br />The liche encounter was easily more confusing, if not more dangerous. (you had to do the dragons all over again if you screwed it up) <br /><br />Then somehow, you had to convince 24 of your closest friends to go to Plane of sky, and fight for hours to get to the 4th island to do your turn in. An all day prospect in the old days, and god help you if someone fell off, lagged, or mommy said they were done with videogames today.<br /><br />Hell even now, you might be hard pressed to get anyone other than good friends to go to PoS for any reason. Not to mention the fact that people solo the Kunark dragons now, so they arent as common as they once were. (and no longer a good alternative to killing naggy and vox) I am Pre-elemental, I cant solo gore to get my book. Even at 65 the original epic is still &quot;difficult&quot; for SOME paladins, and that is content that is 5 years old! <br /><br />Players dont seem to remember anymore that the game was HARD, because of verant&#039;s philosophy, (yay vision! <sup>tm</sup>) and fighting with the rudimentary tools of the day. As a result of the challenge, personal ownership of the character is much deeper than characters of today. CoH is easier, my superhero isnt as valuable to me though as my EQ character, I went through hell to get where I am as a casual player.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									&#171; <i>Last Edit: September 21, 2004, 10:45:50 am by Gabus</i> &#187;
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=139779" target="_blank">Gabus Magelo Profile</a>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
